{"assets":["US Large Cap","Dev ex US","EM","UST","US IG Corp Bond","REITs"],"report":{"title":"Investment Committee Performance Report","period":"Multi-asset endowment portfolio and USD 5m UK equity carve-out  ·  Review period: 31-Jan-2018 to 29-Mar-2019","summary":["• Return objective was not met. The strategic allocation (SAA) delivered an annualised 1.9% against a forward-looking objective of 6.3%, and was held back by the Q4-2018 sell-off in equities and REITs.","• Risk stayed well within tolerance: realised volatility was about 7.7% against the 15% \"medium\" risk budget. However, returns showed negative skew and fat tails, and the portfolio did not beat the 2.35% risk-free MAR, so both Sortino ratios are negative.","• The tactical tilts (TAA) did not add value. Moving defensively after Q4-2018 meant missing the Q1-2019 rebound: the TAA returned about 2.3% versus 4.5% for the SAA in Q1, a 2.2% shortfall.","• The UK equity carve-out lost about 13.9% in USD unhedged. Most of the loss came from the fund itself (-12.5% in GBP); GBP fell about 1.5%. The 50% short-futures hedge (5 contracts of USD 500k) earned about $47.5k and cut the USD loss to about 12.9%."],"keyFigures":[["Annualised mean return",0.01886042,0.00137618,0.06302752,"Below objective"],["Annualised volatility",0.07665441,0.0724309,0.15,"Within tolerance"],["Sharpe ratio (rf 2.35%)",-0.060526,-0.30544724,0,"Negative"],["Sortino ratio (MAR 2.35%, consistent)",-0.08487245,-0.40402594,0,"Negative"],["Sortino ratio (course template)",-0.1542032,-0.72465801,0,"Negative"],["Downside deviation (annualised)",0.05466538,0.05475841,"—",null],["Skewness",-0.34198492,-0.43752479,0,"Negative"],["Excess kurtosis",1.54519863,2.02149864,0,"Fat tails"],["Worst month",-0.04979097,-0.04979097,"—",null],["Cumulative return (15 months)",0.02012091,-0.00135836,"—",null],["Q1-2019 return (TAA live period)",0.04453235,0.02253908,"SAA = benchmark","TAA lagged SAA"]],"carveOut":[["Initial GBP investment",3835826.62063674,"At spot 0.7672 GBP per USD"],["Fund return in GBP (local)",-0.12544356,"Equity risk dominates"],["GBP vs USD currency return",-0.01542002,"GBP weakened against USD"],["Unhedged return in USD",-0.13892924,"Benchmark for the hedge decision"],["50% hedged return in USD",-0.12942823,"Short GBP futures: 5 x USD 500k"],["Hedge value added",0.00950101,"Hedge P&L offsets part of the FX loss"],["Futures P&L (USD)",47505.03008587,null],["GBP/USD annualised volatility",0.08879859,"Currency risk, versus…"],["Fund annualised volatility (GBP)",0.52506755,"…equity risk, which is far larger"],["Hedged vs unhedged USD volatility","52.9% vs 54.7%","Modest risk reduction"]],"findings":["Return objectives — The SAA was built to target about 6.3% a year at 15% volatility. Over a short 15-month window that included the Q4-2018 drawdown (worst month about -5%), it earned 1.9% annualised, below both the objective and the 2.35% risk-free rate. A 15-month window is too short to judge a strategic policy, but the shortfall should be monitored.","Risk tolerance — Realised volatility (about 7–8%) was roughly half the 15% budget, so the portfolio took less risk than its tolerance allowed. Downside risk is what matters: negative skew (about -0.3 for SAA, -0.4 for TAA) and positive excess kurtosis show more frequent large losses than a normal distribution implies. A downside deviation of about 5.5% against the MAR gives negative Sortino ratios for both.","Benchmark: TAA vs SAA — Using the SAA as the policy benchmark, the TAA cut US large caps by 20 percentage points and EM by 7, and added 20 to IG credit and 7 to UST. The tilts were fitted to the Sep–Dec 2018 sell-off, then markets reversed in Q1-2019. The TAA lowered volatility only marginally (7.2% vs 7.7%) while giving up 2.2% of return, so it lowered the Sharpe and Sortino ratios. Tilts optimised on one quarter of crisis data are backward-looking and should be governed by tighter tilt limits and a longer estimation window.","Currency exposure — The UK fund was the main source of loss (-12.5% in GBP), and its volatility is several times that of GBP/USD (about 9%). Currency was a secondary but real drag (-1.5%). The 50% hedge (5 short contracts of USD 500k = USD 2.5m, exactly half the investment) earned about $47.5k and improved the USD result by about 0.95 percentage points. A hedge only removes currency risk, not equity risk, so it cannot protect against the fund's own decline."],"recommendations":"1) Keep the SAA and review it against its 6.3% objective over a full market cycle, not 15 months.   2) Suspend or cap tactical tilts (for example ±10% per asset) until the TAA process shows value out-of-sample; use longer windows than one quarter.   3) Keep the 50% currency hedge as a policy for the GBP carve-out; it lowers FX volatility at low cost. Review the UK fund mandate given its high volatility.   4) Add drawdown and downside-deviation limits to the risk-tolerance framework alongside volatility.","methods":"Methods: monthly returns from index data; annualised return = (1+mean monthly)^12 − 1; volatility = monthly st. dev. x √12; Sortino uses MAR = 2.35% risk-free. The \"consistent\" Sortino converts the MAR to monthly and annualises the downside deviation. Currency futures are priced by covered interest parity with GBP 1.219% / USD 2.684% rates."},"saa":{"corr":[[1,0.899,0.71095,-0.3458515,0.26705,0.6438],[0.899,1,0.8227,-0.319864,0.38375,0.6532],[0.71095,0.8227,1,-0.2530505,0.4127,0.6051],[-0.3458515,-0.319864,-0.2530505,1,0.5043,-0.0238854],[0.26705,0.38375,0.4127,0.5043,1,0.4518],[0.6438,0.6532,0.6051,-0.0238854,0.4518,1]],"er":[0.070929,0.0742635,0.100071,0.0233955,0.0367605,0.067356],"vol":[0.193072,0.2187735,0.3240215,0.1215115,0.0789305,0.276177],"w":[0.32957596,0.1,0.17145983,0.19896421,0.1,0.1],"ret":0.06302752,"pvol":0.15000085,"rf":0.03,"sharpe":0.2201822},"taa":{"start":"2018-09-28","end":"2018-12-31","corr":[[1,0.9852162,0.98669661,0.51489359,-0.33301793,0.47813672],[0.9852162,1.0,0.99996065,0.3